Q1) What is Java?

Java is a high-level, object-oriented and platform-independent programming language developed by Sun Microsystems.

Java follows the principle of "Write Once, Run Anywhere" because Java source code is compiled into bytecode, and this bytecode runs on the Java Virtual Machine, or JVM.

Java is widely used for backend development, enterprise applications, Android-related development, and many other software applications. 

