Q5) What is JRE?       //Java application ko RUN karna.

JRE stands for Java Runtime Environment. It provides the environment and libraries required to run Java applications. It contains the JVM and Java class libraries.

JRE does not contain development tools like the Java compiler. Its main purpose is to provide the runtime environment required to execute Java applications.



