Explain how a Java program works from source code to execution.

First, we write Java source code in a .java file. The JDK provides the javac compiler, which compiles the source code into bytecode stored in a .class file. When we run the application, the JVM loads this bytecode using the Class Loader. The Execution Engine then interprets or JIT-compiles the bytecode into native machine instructions, which are executed by the CPU.

