Q7) What is a class? ( Class ek blueprint/template hai jo define karti hai ki object ke paas kaunsa data aur kaunse behaviors honge.)

A class is a blueprint or template used to create objects. (we can say logical entity)

It defines the properties and behaviors that an object can have.

Class doesnt get any sapace in memory.

class consist Fields + Method + Constructor

For example, Car can be a class containing properties like color and speed and methods like start() and stop().

*************
class Car {

    // Properties / Data       .......fileds
    String color;
    int speed;

    // Behavior / Method
    void start() {
        System.out.println("Car is starting");
    }

    void stop() {
        System.out.println("Car is stopping");
    }
}

public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {

        // Creating object
        Car car1 = new Car();               //Car class ke blueprint se car1 naam ka actual
                                               object create karo.

        // Giving values to properties
        car1.color = "Red";
        car1.speed = 100;

        // Accessing properties
        System.out.println(car1.color);
        System.out.println(car1.speed);

        // Calling methods
        car1.start();
        car1.stop();
    }
}

Output :

Red
100
Car is starting
Car is stopping

