Q15) What is static ?

The static keyword is used for members that belong to the class , rather than to individual objects. A static member is associated with the class, so we generally don't need to create an object to access it. We can access it directly using the class name.

use for memory manegment 

In Static field some information is comman for  all object 
ex. collage name 

Static has single space and single storage

Shared among all object 

not part of an object 


****************Simple example:

class Student {

    // Normal / Instance field
    String name;

    // Static field
    static String college = "ABC College";            ← ONE storage(Ye har object ke andar 
                                                         alag-alag college nahi banata.)
}

public class Main {

    public static void main(String[] args) {

        // Object create kiya
        Student s1 = new Student();

        // Normal field ko object ke through access karte hain
        s1.name = "Jay";

        System.out.println(s1.name);

        // Static field ko class name ke through access karte hain
        System.out.println(Student.college);
    }
}

************Output:
Jay
ABC College

