Q16) Why is OOP important in Java?

OOP stands for Object-Oriented Programming.

It is a programming approach in which we organize software around objects that contain data and behavior.

OOP is important in Java because it helps us organize and manage large Java applications by using classes and objects

It provides features like encapsulation, inheritance, polymorphism, and abstraction

which help make code reusable, maintainable, flexible, and easier to manage.

